					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-78954#post-4071340</guid>
				<title>Trim</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-78954/scp-168#post-4071340</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 29 Nov 2018 16:06:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Voct</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>392303</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>In July of this year, I noticed that this SCP had a needlessly sadistic detail, which was a relic of the different site culture at the time it was written. Specifically, the comment about killing/destroying the SCP if it's not cooperative.</p> <blockquote> <p>Attempts to communicate with SCP-168 after that point were ignored. I suggest that we move it to room 221-D if we want to get anything actually useful out of it. <em>Disassembly should be a last resort, should nothing else succeed in making SCP-168 more compliant.</em></p> </blockquote> <p>I sent a Wikidot PM to the writer, and got no response. In August, I approached a member of rewrite team on IRC, and discussed it with him. He said he would talk to other members of rewrite team.</p> <p>Today (November 29), I noticed that nothing had been done, so I messaged him again, and got his permission to remove that detail.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
